      "content": "thanks for that. for the first part, i really want to lean into that idea of why people see some things as \"revolutionary\" vs \"regressive.\" could you expand on that intro? specifically, can you give me some examples of the specific \"regressive\" or \"stubborn\" arguments that people used to fight against the Civil Rights or Suffragette movements, so the kids can see how those opposing views were framed at the time?",
